<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">buy</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">buy</ansi> command buys an item for sale at a merchant.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

::rows
  <ansi fg="command">buy sword</ansi>              Buy one sword.
  <ansi fg="command">buy 5 iron ingot</ansi>       Buy five iron ingots at once.
  <ansi fg="command">buy sword from kerra</ansi>   Buy from a specific merchant.
::

When buying multiple items, the purchase stops early if you
run out of gold or cannot carry any more.

Secondhand goods are bought by the name <ansi fg="command">list</ansi> shows you.
When two share a name, <ansi fg="command">buy 2.trinket</ansi> buys the second one
listed. Mind the dot: <ansi fg="command">buy 2 trinket</ansi>, with a space,
buys two trinkets. The word <ansi fg="command">bauble</ansi>, which
<ansi fg="command">sell</ansi> accepts for any trinket, does not work here.

Find out more about referring to items by name by typing
<ansi fg="command">help item-names</ansi>.

::rows
<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi>  <ansi fg="command">help list</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help sell</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help item-names</ansi>
::

